    "question": {
      ":question/id": "34888183-bd37-5e93-9a62-37ac6f673b19",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$ be a $5\\times 10$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},{b}_{4},{b}_{5}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=10,$ and since $B$ is formed by $5$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 5+\\text{nullity}(A) & =10 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =10-5 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
